Anitha goes to her own flat.
I am alone in my flat now.
All the rooms are very quiet.
I walk in the living room.
My desk sits near the window.
There is a small plant on the windowsill.
I look in the kitchen.
There are new dishes in the cupboard.
Everything sits very beautifully.
The photo sits on top of the shelf.
I look at my family's photo.
Then I go to the bedroom.
The nice Kochi breeze is coming through the window.
My big bag sits under the bed.
My clothes are in the wardrobe.
There is a new bedsheet on top of the bed.
I lie down on the bed.
I feel very happy now.
This flat is truly my own home.
